OL,3,AEnergy bills to rise by 26% from
OL,4,AJanuary
OL,5,
OL,6,FEnergy bills will soar by 26% for
OL,7,Fmillions of households in January,
OL,8,Funder regulator Ofgem's new price cap.
OL,10,FA typical annual bill will increase by
OL,11,Fabout #37 a month in the first three
OL,12,Fmonths of the new year, although
OL,13,Findividual households costs will depend
OL,14,Fon how much they use at the coldest
OL,15,Ftime of year.
OL,17,FOfgem said that, for a typical
OL,18,Fhousehold paying by direct debit for
OL,19,Fgas and electricity, the rise would
OL,20,Fmean an annual bill would rise from
OL,21,F#1,723 to #2,166 if this level was
OL,22,Fsustained for a year.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
